  "interpretation": "Sample verified in two fresh rootfs, read-only runs and eight fixed-input calls using the current harness synthetic JNI initializer fixture. Python parses its bounded JSON and generates the four-byte first MD5/SHA-1 shared word from complete string field zero plus the 368-byte encoded configuration from complete string field three. The captured configuration and digest inputs are comparison-only; both generated configuration and word equal their captured native counterparts in all calls. Generated decoder output, MD5 key, configuration decryption, SHA-1/RC4 key, RC4 data, parsed selection, material and final native ciphertext retain the parent comparisons and relation ledger. The configuration field is not independently sourced from original Android JNI provider memory: provider pointer/return ownership was not joined, other initializer values and lengths were not varied, and the fixture is synthetic. Android allocator/singleton equivalence, complete standalone signer and ordinary Cronet six-header online acceptance remain unverified. No initializer contents, operands, digest inputs, keys/IVs, plaintext, runtime pointers or operand digests are published."
